  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1047 AM CDT Tue Jun 2 2026\n\nHigh pressure will dominate our forecast through Friday, keeping\ndry and warm conditions in place. Temperatures will gradually warm\nthroughout the week as the ridge axis moves overhead, eventually\nleading to afternoon highs back into the upper 80s. The high\npressure center will start to breakdown this weekend, and mid-\nlevel flow will transition back out of the southwest, re- \nintroducing scattered shower and thunderstorm chances to the \nforecast. Very low rain/storm chances Saturday, less than 20%, but\nbetter moisture will advect in by Sunday, bringing those chances \nup to 40-50%. As mentioned above, temperatures by this point will\nbe back up into the upper 80s, and with increase humidity, it \nwill feel pretty icky outside, so keep this in mind if you have \noutdoor plans this weekend. \n\nThis pattern will continue into at least early next week as\nMiddle TN becomes sandwiched between an expansive area of high \npressure over the gulf and a deepening low over the New England \ncoast. Fortunately, there does not appear to be any organized \nthreat for severe weather. This pattern will favor more of the \nsummertime-like storms that we've been experiencing over the last\nweek or so.",
